---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | FieldLedger"
  description="Master Terms of Service and Customer Subscription Agreement for FieldLedger."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-safety-orange/10 border border-safety-orange/30 text-safety-orange font-mono text-xs font-semibold mb-4">
      SUBSCRIPTION AGREEMENT
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-2">Last updated: August 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed border-t border-carbon-800 pt-6">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">1. Agreement to Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By creating an account, accessing, or using FieldLedger ("the Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you are entering into this agreement on behalf of a company or commercial entity, you represent that you possess the authority to bind such entity.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">2. Scope of Service & Product Boundaries</h2>
        <p>
          FieldLedger is an operational recording, barcode management, photographic documentation, and report generation tool for service contractors.
        </p>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-carbon-800 bg-carbon-900/60 p-4 text-xs text-slate-400">
          <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Notice of Independent Contractor Responsibility:</strong>
          FieldLedger records technician observations and equipment metadata. FieldLedger does not independently inspect, test, certify, or license physical equipment or premises. Service contractors remain solely responsible for ensuring that all work complies with local Authority Having Jurisdiction (AHJ) rules, NFPA codes, EPA rules, and professional trade standards.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">3. Subscriptions, Invoicing & Billing</h2>
        <p>
          Subscriptions are billed in advance on a monthly basis via Stripe. You may cancel your subscription at any time through the self-service Customer Portal. Upon cancellation, access continues until the end of the current billing cycle.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">4. User Content & Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          You retain full ownership of all customer data, equipment barcodes, photographs, and field logs uploaded to the Service. You grant FieldLedger a limited license to host, store, and process your content strictly for the purpose of operating the Service for your account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">5. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, in no event shall FieldLedger, its developers, or affiliates be liable for any indirect, punitive, incidental, special, consequential, or exemplary damages, including without limitation damages for loss of profits, goodwill, or trade licensing penalties resulting from the use or inability to use the service.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
